SUMMARY:Ubud Writers & Readers Festival (UWRF) 2026
LOCATION:Taman Baca Ubud
DESCRIPTION:Southeast Asia’s biggest literary event\, Ubud Writers & Read
 ers Festival (UWRF)\, returns this 22 to 25 October with a powerful progra
 mme of over a hundred separate events. For its 23rd year\, authors\, think
 ers\, journalists\, poets and more will descend upon Ubud for a week of in
 sight and intrigue. The theme this year is ‘Samarasā: Awareness. Empath
 y. Action.’\, which will guide UWRF’s main programme’s many curated 
 conversations and panels. 150 of the region’s most current\, exciting wr
 iters will discuss the transformative power of storytelling and its abilit
 y to mobilise and enlighten individuals\, communities and humanity. As alw
 ays\, the UWRF festival carefully selects its Main Programme speakers\, wh
 ose works\, knowledge and life experiences add poignance\, depth and reali
 ty into each year’s discussions. A highly-anticipated speaker is Tari La
 ng \, author of the memoir ‘ My Neighbour\, The Dictator\,’ in which s
 he recounts her life as a fourteen-year-old girl in 1965 when General Suha
 rto’s coup saw her parents imprisoned without trial\, and how this histo
 ry continues to shape who she is.\n\nMore info: https://www.nowbali.co.id/
 upcoming-events/uwrf-2026/\n\nPlease verify with the organizer before atte
 nding.
URL:https://www.nowbali.co.id/upcoming-events/uwrf-2026/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261022
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261025
END:VEVENT
